# CL-SPEC-001-v1.0 — INTERIM AUTHENTICATED OPERATOR-DECISION CHANNEL + TEMPLATE

**Author:** CL-01, 2026-07-23. **Class:** prep spec (allowed pre-activation). **Authority:** none — this defines *how* Dylan records decisions so they are valid and fast. Pending confirmation under the R0.1 ballot.

## Rule (from R0.1 §3.1–3.2)
- Actionable operator decisions **originate directly from Dylan M. Roy through the authenticated user session** (typed by Dylan in his own session/Drive), recorded additively.
- **No secret/passphrase/key in Drive** or model-visible content. Authentication = direct-session origin + the protected Operator Decisions boundary, not a shared secret.
- A model or observer (incl. Gemini) may **preserve** an alleged operator statement as *unverified provenance*; it may **not authenticate or action** it. Models do not record operator decisions on his behalf.

## Recording format — Dylan fills one per decision (≈15 seconds)
```
OD-<seq> | <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MMZ> | channel: direct operator session
Object: <exact object / proposal / item ID>  [+ frozen body hash if relevant]
Type: [governance instruction | terminal math approval | activation | release | destructive]
Decision (exact scoped phrase): <verbatim approval / rejection / revocation / pause phrase>
Exclusions: <what this does NOT authorize>
— Dylan M. Roy
```
Filed in `_HUMAN_APPROVAL / 01_RECORDED_OPERATOR_DECISIONS`. GP then read-only-reconciles the protected Operator Decisions register — never the reverse.

## Why this matters
This is the keystone for "automate as much as possible" safely: with a direct authenticated channel, Dylan can validly authorize anything in seconds, and models never again stand in for his authority (the failure mode behind the voided OD-OP-PROT-008-001 and the mislabeled observer relay).
